poemTitle: "Meaningful_Christmas_by_Eila"
author: "Eila Webster"
bgTheme: "antiquewhite"
endOfYear: false
---
<div class="full-width">
<poem-grid :title="poemTitle" :author="author" :theme="bgTheme">

  <!-- Header Section -->
  <img src="/images/poems/happy-2020.png" alt="" slot="header-tl" />
  <img src="/images/poems/happy-2020.png" alt="" slot="header-tr" />

  <!-- Column 1 Images (15%) -->
  <div slot="col-1-images">
    <!-- No side images -->
  </div>

  <!-- Column 2 Text -->
  <div slot="col-2-text">
    <p>
      Meaningful Christmas	Meaningful Christmas	Meaningful Christmas	Meaningful Christmas
      The old year’s ending and thoughts return
      to the Christmas we knew long ago
      Before commercial bodies took hold
    </p>

    <p>
      With lavish gifts and tinsel show.
      *****
      Christmas held some meaning then
      Singing Carols, hearts warmed by praise
    </p>

    <p>
      Christmas greetings are no longer used
      recently changed to Happy Holidays.
      *****
      From late September in all the Stores
    </p>

    <p>
      Christmas gifts glitter to catch the eye
      As youngsters see the gadgets galore
      that they want their kinfolk to buy.
      *****
    </p>

    <p>
      It is like a competition for parents
      All wanting the most expensive gift
      The old year’s ending and thoughts return
      Stretching and spending beyond means
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Column 3 Middle Images -->
  <div slot="col-3-images">
    <!-- No center images -->
  </div>

  <!-- Column 4 Text -->
  <div slot="col-4-text">
    <p>
      Never giving a real thought to thrift
      *****
      Things then begin spinning out of control
      New Year brings a real mess of debt
    </p>

    <p>
      Trying to impress in this modern world
      Can land you with lots of regret
      *****
      What is wrong with a simple meal
    </p>

    <p>
      A small gift picked from the tree
      When generations joined in party games
      the joy there, was plain to see
      *****
    </p>

    <p>
      You can’t delete the Real Christmas
      Nor the bright shining star in the sky
      GOD keeps on sending us precious gifts
      the ones that no money can buy.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Column 5 Images (15%) -->
  <div slot="col-5-images">
    <!-- No side images -->
  </div>

</poem-grid>
</div>
